# VerticalStackedBarChart

## Overview

A complete vertical stacked bar chart component that composes `ChartHeader`, `ChartLegend`, `DataDisplay`, `VerticalStackedBarGroup`, and `ChartFooter` into a cohesive data visualization. All tokens (colours, typography, spacing, DataVis palette) come from the CSS `@layer brand` cascade — no `modes` prop, no runtime JS resolver.

**This component follows the Organized Props Pattern** — Layer 2 parent props (`data`, `width`, `chartHeader`, etc.) plus Layer 3 child configs (`chartHeaderConfig`, `chartLegendConfig`, `barGroupConfig`, `chartFooterConfig`, `dataDisplayConfig`) grouped by the child component they configure.

## Figma Reference

- **Node ID**: `133:2318`
- **Design File**: DataVis-Components
- **Figma URL**: https://www.figma.com/design/uA5ExvS0cNXbDEKzT9Rnrt/DataVis-Components?node-id=133-2318

## Architecture

```
VerticalStackedBarChart (flex container, vertical layout)
├── ChartHeader (conditional, when chartHeader=true)
│   ├── ChartTitle
│   └── ChartSubtitle
├── ChartLegend (conditional, when chartLegend=true)
│   └── ChartKey[] (6 items for categorical colors)
│       ├── Circle indicator (categorical color)
│       └── Label
├── DataDisplay (conditional, when dataDisplay=true)
│   ├── contentLeft
│   │   ├── mainLabel (inline typography + optional InfoIcon)
│   │   └── DataHead (DataLead + SupportingData + SupportingLabel)
│   └── contentRight (DataBadgeSemantic)
├── VerticalStackedBarGroup
│   ├── YAxis (optional, when yAxis=true)
│   │   └── ChartAxisTick (for each tick value)
│   ├── AvgLine (optional, when avgLine=true)
│   └── contentWrapper (flex, space-between)
│       └── VerticalStackedBar[] (D3-scaled heights)
│           ├── topOutsideLabel (optional total)
│           ├── stackedBars (pill radius container)
│           │   └── shapeRect[1-6] (colored segments)
│           └── categoryLabel
└── ChartFooter (conditional, when chartFooter=true)
    ├── source (inline typography tokens)
    └── notes (inline typography tokens)
```

## Canonical Default Render

> **This is what consumers should get when they request a `VerticalStackedBarChart` without supplying extra detail.** It is the spec: the `Default` story in `VerticalStackedBarChart.stories.tsx` matches this exactly, and any future change to the canonical baseline must update the story, this section, and the meta `docs.description` together.

### What's ON by default

| Part                            | Default                 | Why                                                                                                            |
| ------------------------------- | ----------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `ChartHeader`                   | **ON**                  | Title + subtitle anchor the chart so the reader knows what they're looking at                                  |
| `ChartLegend`                   | **ON**                  | Stacked-series charts always need the per-series colour key (segment identity isn't legible otherwise)         |
| `barGroupConfig.categoryLabels` | **ON**                  | The X-axis identifies each bar                                                                                 |
| `barGroupConfig.yAxis`          | **ON** (opt-in — prop defaults to `false`) | Quantitative reference for the bar totals; ticks share the bar group's D3 scale. The canonical baseline turns it on explicitly since most product charts want it |
| `barGroupConfig.hoverBadge`     | **ON**                  | Cursor-following `DataBadge` for per-segment value reveal — always paired with `hoverType: "individual"` below |
| `barGroupConfig.hoverType`      | **`"individual"`**      | Per-segment focus on hover so the hoverBadge surfaces the specific segment's value, not just the bar total     |
| `ChartFooter`                   | **ON**                  | Slot for source / footnote annotations                                                                         |
| `interactive`                   | **ON** (default `true`) | Bars / segments receive hover / click / focus handlers                                                         |
| `barGroupConfig.barWidth`       | **`"M"`**               | Default bar width                                                                                              |
| `barGroupConfig.barHeightMode`  | **`"relative"`**        | Real-magnitude stacking; switch to `"fullHeight"` only for 100% stacked / composition charts                   |
| `width`                         | **`520`**               | Chart width in pixels — comfortable Storybook frame width (the prop's own bare default is `328`); consumers should override to match their layout |

### What's OFF by default (opt-in only)

| Part                                                  | When to enable                                                                                                                                    |
| ----------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `dataDisplay`                                         | Only when the chart is paired with a primary KPI / summary surface that benefits from a static or hover-driven `DataDisplay` block above the bars |
| `barGroupConfig.topLabels`                            | Only when bar widths are wide enough (`barWidth: "L"` and above) and the total above each bar adds value                                          |
| `barGroupConfig.avgLine`                              | Comparison against the dataset mean bar-total or a fixed threshold                                                                                |
| `barGroupConfig.barHeightMode: "fullHeight"`          | 100% stacked / composition charts (market share, allocation, mix shift) where every bar should reach full height and segments are proportions     |
| Non-default `hoverType` (`"group"` / `"categorical"`) | Switch to `"group"` when the bar-as-unit is the right interaction target, or `"categorical"` (same series across bars) for series comparison      |
| `animated`                                            | Datasets that change at runtime (filters, scenario toggles)                                                                                       |
| `seriesOrder` / `valueFormat` / `dataSort`            | Domain-specific ordering / formatting / sorting needs                                                                                             |
| `categoryLabelConfig` overrides                       | Long category names that need word / line-clamp tuning                                                                                            |
| `accessibility.enabled`                               | Production charts (always opt in for shipped charts; off in this default for the rendered Storybook demo)                                         |

### Minimal canonical example

```tsx
<VerticalStackedBarChart
  data={canonicalData}
  width={520}
  chartHeader
  chartLegend
  chartFooter
  chartHeaderConfig={{
    chartTitleValue: "Quarterly revenue by product.",
    chartSubtitleValue: "Stacked segments show each product's contribution to total revenue.",
  }}
  barGroupConfig={{
    categoryLabels: true,
    yAxis: true,
    yAxisConfig: { tickCount: 6 },
    barWidth: "M",
    hoverBadge: true,
    hoverType: "individual",
  }}
  chartFooterConfig={{
    annotationLeftValue: "Source: Jio.",
    annotationRightValue: "FY 2024.",
  }}
/>
```

> **Authoring rule:** when a consumer (human or LLM) asks for "a VerticalStackedBarChart" without further detail, render the example above — _not_ the `Anatomy` story (everything turned on at once). Anatomy exists as a reference; the default is what ships in real product surfaces.

## Import

