### Interactive Legend (per-series hover value)

`chartLegendConfig.interactiveDataHead` drives auto-generated legend items' DataHead lead values from hover. Behaviour depends on `barGroupConfig.hoverType`:

- **`"individual"` / `"categorical"`** (segment-level hover): `segmentIndex` is set on hover, so only that one series' legend item updates — the others keep their static `dataHeadConfig` value.
- **`"group"`** (whole-bar hover): no single series is identified, but the hovered category is known (`hoverData.label`). The chart looks up every series' value for that category from `data` and updates **all** legend items simultaneously — mirroring `VerticalMultiBarChart`'s group-hover behaviour. This does not work for an aggregated "Others" bar (from overflow grouping), since there's no single source row to look up — the legend simply keeps its static values in that case.

```tsx
<VerticalStackedBarChart
  data={data}
  chartLegend={true}
  chartLegendConfig={{
    dataHead: true,
    dataHeadConfig: { dataLeadValue: 1234, supportingLabelValue: "Total" },
    interactiveDataHead: true,
  }}
  barGroupConfig={{
    hoverType: "group", // "individual" | "categorical" also supported
  }}
/>
```

