## Design Tokens Used

All tokens come from the CSS `@layer brand` cascade. No runtime JS resolver.

| Property           | CSS Custom Property                          | Layer         | Description                                            |
| ------------------ | -------------------------------------------- | ------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |
| Section Gap        | `var(--VerticalStackedBarChart-gap, var(--Spacing-5))` | `base`  | Gap between header, legend, chart, footer — two-layer override hook |
| Categorical Colors | `var(--DataVis-Categorical-Bold-{1..6})`     | `brand`       | Injected by `generateDataVisCSS` → `useStyleInjection` |
| Surface tokens     | `var(--Surface-*)`, `var(--Text-*)`          | `brand`       | Injected by `useBrandCSSNew` → `@layer brand`          |
| Typography         | `var(--Body-M-FontSize)`, `var(--Label-S-*)` | `semantic`    | Role-explicit tokens from `packages/tokens/`           |

## Legend Auto-Generation

When `chartLegend` is `true` and no `chartLegendConfig.items` are provided, the component auto-generates legend items:

1. **From segment labels**: Uses the first category's segment labels and categorical colors
2. **From segment colors**: Uses custom colors if provided on segments
3. **Default**: Creates 6 items with "Category name" labels and `categorical/bold/1-6` colors

This ensures the legend matches the stacked bar colors.

The legend automatically hides when only a single series is detected (non-stacked data), since a one-item legend is redundant. It reappears when 2+ series are present. Manually provided `chartLegendConfig.items` are always shown regardless of series count.

Auto-generated items also carry `type`, `dataHead`, and `dataHeadConfig` from `chartLegendConfig` (when set), and — with `interactiveDataHead: true` — hover drives the legend items' DataHead lead value(s) live, for any `barGroupConfig.hoverType`. See [Interactive Legend](#interactive-legend-per-series-hover-value) above.

## Height Behavior

The `height` prop controls the **total chart height**, not just the bar group. The VerticalStackedBarGroup automatically stretches to fill the remaining space after header, legend, DataDisplay, and footer.

### How It Works

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ ChartHeader (natural height)            │
├─────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ ChartLegend (natural height)            │
├─────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ DataDisplay (natural height, optional)  │
├─────────────────────────────────────────┤
│                                         │
│ VerticalStackedBarGroup (flex: 1, fills)│
│                                         │
├─────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ ChartFooter (natural height)            │
└─────────────────────────────────────────┘
       ↑                                ↑
       └────── Total height prop ───────┘
```

### Usage Examples

```tsx
// Fixed 500px chart - bar group fills remaining space
<VerticalStackedBarChart
  data={data}
  height={500}
  chartHeader={true}
  chartFooter={true}
/>

// Compact 280px chart for dashboards
<VerticalStackedBarChart
  data={data}
  height={280}
  chartHeader={true}
  chartFooter={false}
  chartLegend={false}
/>

// Bars only - fills full height
<VerticalStackedBarChart
  data={data}
  height={300}
  chartHeader={false}
  chartFooter={false}
  chartLegend={false}
/>
```

### Key Benefits

1. **Predictable sizing**: Chart always respects the specified height
2. **Automatic stretching**: Bar group expands to fill available space
3. **Consistent layouts**: Same chart height regardless of which sections are visible
4. **Responsive-friendly**: Use percentage heights for fluid layouts

## Hover Interaction

The chart supports hover interaction with automatic dimming of non-hovered bars.

### Color & Opacity States

| State                              | Color Token                 | Opacity | Description                   |
| ---------------------------------- | --------------------------- | ------- | ----------------------------- |
| **Default** (nothing hovered)      | `categorical/bold/{index}`  | `1`     | Original vibrant colors       |
| **Highlighted** (this bar hovered) | `categorical/bold/{index}`  | `1`     | Stays vibrant                 |
| **Dimmed** (another bar hovered)   | `categorical/hover/{index}` | `0.2`   | Muted color + reduced opacity |

### Hover Types

| Type            | Description                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 |
| --------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `"group"`       | All segments in a bar highlight together; other bars dim                                                                                                                                                                                                    |
| `"individual"`  | Only the hovered segment highlights; other segments and bars dim                                                                                                                                                                                            |
| `"categorical"` | Same segment index across ALL bars highlights together; e.g., hovering on "Product A" in any bar highlights all "Product A" segments. The hit area resolves the segment from cursor Y position, so detection works in gaps between bars without flickering. |

### Transition Tokens

All hover transitions use design tokens from the `hoverAnimation` collection:

- **Easing**: `"easing"` - Cubic-bezier timing function
- **Duration**: `"duration"` - Transition time (e.g., 200ms for "Moderate" mode)
- **Dim Opacity**: `"dimOpacity"` - Opacity for dimmed bars (default: 0.2)

