## Entry Animation

When `animated={true}`, bars grow from zero height to their full D3-scaled height on first load, staggered one after another.

### Enabling Entry Animation

```tsx
<VerticalStackedBarChart data={data} animated={true} />
```

### How It Works

1. On first render, all bar heights are set to 0
2. After the first paint, bar heights transition to their D3-scaled values
3. Each bar has a staggered delay (`index × offsetDelay`), so they appear one after another
4. Duration and easing come from the `enterAnimation` Figma token collection

Powered by the shared `useEntryAnimation` hook. See `packages/datavis/src/hooks/useEntryAnimation.ts` for the full token resolution chain and integration pattern for other chart types.

### Combined with Other Features

```tsx
<VerticalStackedBarChart
  data={data}
  animated={true}
  interactive={true}
  barGroupConfig={{
    yAxis: true,
    topLabels: true,
    hoverBadge: true,
  }}
/>

```

### Overflow Re-entry Behaviour

When `overflowType` is `"truncated"` (the default) and `labelWidth` is `"fluid"`, bars that don't fit on smaller screens are trimmed from the right. If the screen later becomes wider and those bars reappear, they are rendered at their full height **instantly** — no entry or segment animation is replayed. This prevents a visual "expand from the middle" artefact that CSS transitions can cause on newly mounted elements.

Internally, `VerticalStackedBarGroup` tracks the previous `scaledData.length` via a ref. When new bars appear at indices beyond the previous count (and the initial entry animation has already settled), the component passes `disableTransitions={true}` to those `VerticalStackedBar` instances, which sets all CSS `transition` properties to `"none"`.

## Data Transition Animation

When `animated={true}` and the `data` prop changes after the chart has loaded, bars smoothly transition from their current heights to new heights. The AvgLine (when visible) also slides up or down to its recalculated position in sync. This uses the shared `useDataTransition` hook alongside entry animation.

### How It Works

1. On first render, entry animation plays (bars grow from zero)
2. After entry animation settles, the `transitionAnimation` tokens take over
3. Any subsequent data changes trigger smooth CSS transitions on bar heights
4. Bars update in a staggered wave pattern (left to right)
5. Individual segments within stacked bars also animate their proportional sizing, with per-bar stagger matching the bar height stagger
6. AvgLine smoothly slides to its new vertical position using `transitionAnimation` easing and duration

### Usage

```tsx
const [data, setData] = useState(initialData);

// Data changes trigger smooth animated transitions
<VerticalStackedBarChart
  data={data}
  animated={true}
/>


// Later — update data, bars animate smoothly
<button onClick={() => setData(newData)}>Update Data</button>
```

### Design Tokens

| Property     | Token Name    | Collection            | Fallback                       |
| ------------ | ------------- | --------------------- | ------------------------------ |
| Easing       | `easing`      | `transitionAnimation` | `cubic-bezier(0.5, 0, 0.3, 1)` |
| Duration     | `duration`    | `transitionAnimation` | `400ms`                        |
| Offset Delay | `offsetDelay` | `transitionAnimation` | `60ms`                         |
| Motion Mode  | `mode`        | `transitionAnimation` | `Moderate`                     |

See `packages/datavis/src/hooks/useDataTransition.ts` for the full hook implementation.

### Data-Change Layout Snap

When data changes cause siblings (e.g., ChartLegend) to re-render at a different height, `barGroupAnimated` could produce a compound double-animation (its own height transition + bar height transitions). Two mechanisms prevent this:

1. **Instant height snap** — A `useLayoutEffect` detects `data` prop changes and reads the new `barGroupWrapper` height before the browser paints. The height is applied imperatively with `transition: none` and a forced reflow, so the container snaps to its final size instantly. `barGroupTransition` is preserved for non-data-driven layout changes (e.g., external resize).

2. **Pixel height pass-through** — `VerticalStackedBarGroup` receives `barGroupTargetHeight` (a number) as its `height` prop instead of `"100%"`. This bypasses the component's internal ResizeObserver chain, so D3 recalculates with the correct container height in the same synchronous render. The result is zero-frame delay: bars get their final `barHeight` values before the first paint.

| Scenario                            | barGroupAnimated height                       | VerticalStackedBarGroup height               |
| ----------------------------------- | --------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------- |
| Data change (segment count, values) | Snaps instantly via `useLayoutEffect`         | Receives pixel value directly                |
| Initial render (no measurement yet) | Falls back to `"100%"`                        | Falls back to `"100%"` (ResizeObserver path) |
| External resize (non-data-driven)   | Transitions smoothly via `barGroupTransition` | Receives updated pixel value                 |

## Accessibility

Wrapped by `ChartAccessibility` (enabled by default). This chart has **full accessibility wiring**, including:

| Feature               | Implementation                                                                                                                                                                   |
| --------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **ARIA wrapper**      | `role="figure"`, `aria-label`, `aria-describedby` with auto summary + data table                                                                                                 |
| **ARIA live region**  | `aria-live="polite"` announces `"{category}, {segmentLabel}: {value}, {pct}% of total"` on hover/focus via `useChartAccessibility` (which debounces through `useAriaLiveRegion`) |
| **Roving tabindex**   | Single tab stop — Arrow Left/Right navigates bars, Home/End jump to first/last via `useRovingTabIndex`                                                                           |
| **Bar semantics**     | `aria-roledescription="data point"`, positional label embedded in `aria-label` (e.g., "bar 1 of 10")                                                                             |
| **Controls linking**  | `aria-controls` on each bar points to DataDisplay (when enabled)                                                                                                                 |
| **Decorative hiding** | YAxis, AvgLine, HoverBadge all `aria-hidden="true"`                                                                                                                              |
| **Legend structure**  | ChartLegend rendered as `role="list"` with `role="listitem"` entries                                                                                                             |

No additional consumer configuration needed — all features activate automatically when `accessibility.enabled` is `true` (the default).

