## Sparse Data Edge Case

When the chart receives only 1-3 category entries, `VerticalStackedBarGroup` automatically renders grey placeholder bars alongside the real stacked bars to indicate that more data is expected. The total bar count is always 5 (real + dummy). No additional props are needed — the behavior is automatic.

- **4+ categories**: Normal rendering
- **1-3 categories**: Real stacked bars (left) + grey dummy bars (right, count = 5 − real), first dummy matches last real bar's height and is labeled "No entries yet"
- **0 categories**: Empty chart

```tsx
// 1 category → automatically shows 4 grey placeholder bars
<VerticalStackedBarChart
  data={[
    { category: "Jan", series: "Product A", value: 45 },
    { category: "Jan", series: "Product B", value: 35 },
  ]}
  chartHeader={true}
  chartHeaderConfig={{ chartTitleValue: "Early Data" }}
  barGroupConfig={{ yAxis: true }}
/>

```

See [VerticalStackedBarGroup.md — Sparse Data Edge Case](../../groups/VerticalStackedBarGroup/VerticalStackedBarGroup.md#sparse-data-edge-case-1-3-entries) and `packages/datavis/src/utils/sparseDataUtils.ts` for full details.

